abstract: |-
  This learning module, developed by the HEP Software Foundation (HSF), explores how to build a CI/CD workflow, guiding participants through the development of automated processes using GitHub Actions and Gitea Actions.

  After completing this module, participants will be able to:

  - Write scripts with appropriate exit codes.
  - Build flexible and reusable CI/CD workflows using GitHub Actions.
  - Configure and manage workflow jobs using YAML.
  - Understand how GitHub Actions runners execute jobs and access repository code.
  - Use matrices, dependencies, and artifacts to create efficient and scalable workflows.
  - Protect secrets and sensitive information while allowing workflows to run securely.
